      "explanation": "<p>Cu<sup>2+</sup> and Ni<sup>2+</sup> ions belong to Group II and Group IV respectively.</p>\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3xb1ktk/925df3ad-9a20-40db-aec3-efcc765d6884/51d6e990-e29b-11ec-8ea3-fd6d660fc854/file-1l3xb1ktl.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l3xb1ktk/925df3ad-9a20-40db-aec3-efcc765d6884/51d6e990-e29b-11ec-8ea3-fd6d660fc854/file-1l3xb1ktl.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2018 (Online) 16th April Morning Slot Chemistry - d and f Block Elements Question 203 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l3xb1ktk/925df3ad-9a20-40db-aec3-efcc765d6884/51d6e990-e29b-11ec-8ea3-fd6d660fc854/file-1l3xb1ktl.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l3xb1ktk/925df3ad-9a20-40db-aec3-efcc765d6884/51d6e990-e29b-11ec-8ea3-fd6d660fc854/file-1l3xb1ktl.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3xb1ktk/925df3ad-9a20-40db-aec3-efcc765d6884/51d6e990-e29b-11ec-8ea3-fd6d660fc854/file-1l3xb1ktl.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l3xb1ktk/925df3ad-9a20-40db-aec3-efcc765d6884/51d6e990-e29b-11ec-8ea3-fd6d660fc854/file-1l3xb1ktl.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l3xb1ktk/925df3ad-9a20-40db-aec3-efcc765d6884/51d6e990-e29b-11ec-8ea3-fd6d660fc854/file-1l3xb1ktl.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l3xb1ktk/925df3ad-9a20-40db-aec3-efcc765d6884/51d6e990-e29b-11ec-8ea3-fd6d660fc854/file-1l3xb1ktl.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p>Group II sulphides precipitated out even under low concentration of sulphides, while Group IV sulphides require higher concentration of sulphides. To fulfill this reaction condition, dil. HCl is chosen in Group II reagents and NH<sub>4</sub>OH is chosen in Group IV reagents.</p>"
